<< lib/java/implementations/java/lang/JavaStringMethods.sleela
   The java.lang.String instance methods for built-in SLeeLa Strings.
   When a method is called on a String value (s.length(), "x".equals(y)),
   semantic analysis binds the call to the static method of the same name here
   and passes the receiver as the first argument, self. Either runtime String
   kind is accepted (a plain legacy String or a VM-owned Java UTF-16 String),
   indexes count UTF-16 code units as in Java, and String results are plain
   whenever the text has a plain form (JavaText.plainIfRepresentable).
   Exceptions carry the JDK 25 messages. Case mapping uses the per-code-point
   tables of java.lang.Character plus the German sharp s (toUpperCase gives
   SS); the final-sigma and Turkish dotted-i special cases of the JDK are not
   applied. Regex members (matches, split, replaceAll, replaceFirst), the
   Locale forms, streams (chars, codePoints, lines) and the static members of
   java.lang.String are not provided here. >>
#sleela 3.0
import java.jdk-25.java.lang;
material;

class JavaStringMethods {
  < ---- Descriptive metadata (version 1.11 nested-friendly accessors) ---- >
  << Eleven catalogued attributes with getter/setter pairs, so a GUI, loader,
     or catalog can read and (where appropriate) override this record.
     Values are faithful to the subject's real origin where publicly known. >>
